Path -- An SVG path
*******************

Description
===========

An SVG path. It follows the syntax of SVG paths, except successive commands
must be grouped together in a list called PointList.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : c=Circle{Radius=>0.1,"fill"=>"black"};                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : v1=gNode([0,0],c,Draggable=>true); v2=gNode([0,1],c,Draggable=>true);   |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|v3=gNode([2,1],c,Draggable=>true); v4=gNode([1,2],c,Draggable=>true);        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : gList(Path{{"M",v1,"C",v2,v3,v4}},v1,v2,v3,v4)                          |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = GraphicsList{cache => CacheTable{}                                      |
|                  Contents => {Path{cache => CacheTable{}                    |
|                                    PointList => {M, GraphicsCoordinate v1,  |
|                                    style => MutableHashTable{}              |
|                  style => MutableHashTable{}                                |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : GraphicsList                                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                                                             |
|                                                                       }, v1,|
|C, GraphicsCoordinate v2, GraphicsCoordinate v3, GraphicsCoordinate v4}      |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|           }                                                                 |
|v2, v3, v4}                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

For the programmer
==================

The object *note Path: Path, is an instance of the type *note GraphicsType:
GraphicsType,, with ancestor classes *note GraphicsPoly: GraphicsPoly, < *note
GraphicsObject: GraphicsObject, < *note GraphicsAncestor: GraphicsAncestor, <
*note HashTable: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, < *note Thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in VectorGraphics.m2:1880:0.

File: VectorGraphics.info, Node: Perspective, Next: place, Prev: Path, Up: Top

Perspective -- Set the amount of perspective
********************************************

Description
===========

A 4x4 matrix that is applied to 3d coordinates for perspective. One can instead
provide a real number $p$, which is equivalent to placing the screen centered
at $z=0$ and the viewer at $(0,0,p)$. Only has an effect if in the outermost
*note GraphicsObject: GraphicsObject,.

For the programmer
==================

The object *note Perspective: Perspective, is a *note symbol:
(Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in VectorGraphics.m2:1880:0.

File: VectorGraphics.info, Node: place, Next: plot2d, Prev: Perspective, Up: Top

place -- Position a point relative to two other points
******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        place ( p1, p2, a, b )

Description
===========

Gives a point situated at position a along the line (p1,p2) in units where they
are at distance 1, and at position b orthogonally to it. Only makes sense in
2d.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : (p1,p2)=apply(([-1,-1],[1,1]),coord ->                                  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|gNode(coord,Circle{Radius=>0.1,"fill"=>"red","stroke"=>"black"},Draggable=>  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|true));                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : gList(Polygon{{p1,place(p1,p2,0.7,0.3),p2,place(p1,p2,0.7,-0.3)}},p1,p2 |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = GraphicsList{cache => CacheTable{}                                      |
|                  Contents => {Polygon{cache => CacheTable{}                 |
|                                       PointList => {GraphicsCoordinate p1,  |
|                                       style => MutableHashTable{}           |
|                  style => MutableHashTable{}                                |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : GraphicsList                                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|)                                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|place (GraphicsCoordinate p1, GraphicsCoordinate p2, .7, .3),                |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|GraphicsCoordinate p2, place (GraphicsCoordinate p1, GraphicsCoordinate p2,  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                   }                                                         |
|         }, p1, p2}                                                          |
|.7, -.3)}                                                                    |
